<title>SOUTH AFRICA: INGWE COMPLETES TAKEOVER OF AUSTRALIA'S ACM.</title>
<headline>INGWE COMPLETES TAKEOVER OF AUSTRALIA'S ACM.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ingwe Coal Corporation Ltd said on Friday it had completed its acquisition of 100 percent of Coal Mines Australia Ltd (CMAL).</p>
<p>Ingwe announced early in October that it had acquired 96.3 percent of CMAL for 800 million rand.</p>
<p>Ingwe said in a statement that it had acquired the remaining 3.7 percent from existing CMAL management.</p>
<p>It said the total cost of the transaction including the recapitalization of CMAL amounted to A$200 million.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
